Fix an integer \(\beta\ge 1\), a common Bernoulli treatment probability \(p\in(0,1)\), and \(B>0\).  For each index \(t\), let \(n_t\) and \(d_t\) be positive integers such that \(d_t\mid n_t\), put
\[
m_t:=\frac{n_t}{d_t},
\]
and let \(G_t\) be the directed graph on \(V_{n_t}\) in which \(j\to i\) exactly when both units are active and \(j\) and \(i\) have the same integer quotient after division by \(d_t\), so active units form complete directed blocks with self-loops and inactive units are isolated.  Let the assignment design at every \(t\) be the product Bernoulli design with common probability \(p\), as in \(\cref{obj:ass:bernoulli-design}\).  Write
\[
A_d
:=
\sum_{r=1}^{\bar\beta_d}
\binom{d}{r}\frac{\Delta_r(p)^2}{\{p(1-p)\}^r}.
\]
Then, for every \(t\),
\[
R_t^{\mathrm{loc,lin}}
=
\frac{B^2A_{d_t}}{m_t}
=
\frac{B^2d_tA_{d_t}}{n_t}.
\]

For local linear weights \(w\in\mathcal E_t^{\mathrm{loc,lin}}\), put \(Z_S:=\prod_{j\in S}Z_j\) and, for each active block \(V_b\),
\[
\Psi_{b,t}(w)
:=
\max_{\substack{(\varepsilon_i,S_i)_{i\in V_b}\\
\varepsilon_i\in\{-1,1\},\ S_i\subseteq V_b,\ |S_i|\le \bar\beta_{d_t}}}
\mathbb E_Z\!\left[
\left(
\sum_{i\in V_b}
\varepsilon_i
\left\{
w_{i,t}(Z_{b(i)})Z_{S_i}
-
\mathbf 1\{S_i\ne\varnothing\}
\right\}
\right)^2
\right].
\]
For every \(t\) and every \(w\in\mathcal E_t^{\mathrm{loc,lin}}\),
\[
\sup_{c\in\mathcal M_t(G_t)}
\mathbb E_Z\!\left[(\widehat\tau_{w,t}-\tau_{n_t})^2\right]
=
\frac{B^2}{n_t^2}\sum_{b=1}^{m_t}\Psi_{b,t}(w),
\]
and, for every block \(V_b\),
\[
d_t^2A_{d_t}\le \Psi_{b,t}(w).
\]

For any sequence \(w_t\in\mathcal E_t^{\mathrm{loc,lin}}\),
\[
\frac{
\sup_{c\in\mathcal M_t(G_t)}
\mathbb E_Z\!\left[(\widehat\tau_{w_t,t}-\tau_{n_t})^2\right]
}{
B^2A_{d_t}/m_t
}
\longrightarrow 1
\]
if and only if
\[
\frac{1}{m_td_t^2A_{d_t}}
\sum_{b=1}^{m_t}
\left\{\Psi_{b,t}(w_t)-d_t^2A_{d_t}\right\}
\longrightarrow 0.
\]
Moreover, the sufficient representer condition
\[
\frac{1}{n_tA_{d_t}}
\sum_{i\in V_{n_t}}
\mathbb E_Z\!\left[
\left\{
w_{i,t}(Z_{b(i)})-g_{d_t}(Z_{b(i)})
\right\}^2
\right]
\longrightarrow 0
\]
implies
\[
\frac{
\sup_{c\in\mathcal M_t(G_t)}
\mathbb E_Z\!\left[(\widehat\tau_{w_t,t}-\tau_{n_t})^2\right]
}{
B^2A_{d_t}/m_t
}
\longrightarrow 1.
\]

If \(d_t\to\infty\), then there exists a sequence \(w_t\in\mathcal E_t^{\mathrm{loc,lin}}\) such that
\[
\frac{
\sup_{c\in\mathcal M_t(G_t)}
\mathbb E_Z\!\left[(\widehat\tau_{w_t,t}-\tau_{n_t})^2\right]
}{
B^2A_{d_t}/m_t
}
\longrightarrow 1,
\]
and, for all sufficiently large \(t\),
\[
\frac{1}{n_tA_{d_t}}
\sum_{i\in V_{n_t}}
\mathbb E_Z\!\left[
\left\{
w_{i,t}(Z_{b(i)})-g_{d_t}(Z_{b(i)})
\right\}^2
\right]
=2.
\]
For every permutation \(\pi:V_{n_t}\to V_{n_t}\) that preserves block membership, meaning \(b(\pi(i))=b(i)\) for every \(i\), the corresponding relabeled normalized average squared distance from the complete-block SNIPE score is also equal to \(2\) for all sufficiently large \(t\).

